{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
  "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: May I ask you whether there are statutes in various States that allow an officer to get a no-knock warrant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, when there's probable cause to enter, there's no presumption of innocence, is there, or am I wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MORAN",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "probable cause is a standard at somewhere around 50 percent,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have any empirical basis for your statement that many warrants are executed and they don't find anything?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Timothy A. Baughman",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BAUGHMAN: The entry was lawful."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baughman",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All I'm asking the Court to decide is that causation is required before the exclusionary rule is implemented, and physical evidence found within a proper search of -- search of proper scope, pursuant to the warrant, that that is not causally connected to the -- to the knock-and- announce violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baughman",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the assumption has been, if there's a knock-and-announce violation, you exclude the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baughman",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think to not accept causation as a requirement, which I think this Court has always done -- as I said at the outset, this Court has said that implementation of the exclusionary rule is premised on the evidence being the product of the police misconduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David B. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The knock-and-announce rule, unlike the warrant and probable cause requirements, does not protect the individual's privacy interest in the items to be searched, and does not relate to the officer's authority to conduct the search and obtain the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You just are looking at the harms that his being there in that room without announcing might bring about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is this incentive inherent in the circumstances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, what reason do we have to believe that this incentive inherent in circumstances is ever going to work in the absence of an exclusionary rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, I would -- I would disagree with that. And I would point the Court, in particular, to a recent case out of the Seventh Circuit, Jones versus Wilhelm. The seventh circuit has announced the position -- it decided the position that we advocate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1360",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4a3f5b1f521459f5b8cfb491baad1ca88c7ed93ede01a0c35967ebb60f2573ba",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a3f5b1f5214-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought the Government's distinction was based on the fact that they were arrest cases."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
